soc: sunxi: h713-arisc: crust - watch it while it runs

crust has no watchdog while the system is awake, and this driver set
->running once at the handshake and never looked again. A crust that
hung made every HDMI command wait out its timeout, up to 2 s each, and
every later standby was refused only in noirq; a crust that restarted
through an exception lost its EDID state and nobody said why.

A delayed work looks at the contract page every 10 s, and prepare and a
command that timed out look at once:

- a heartbeat that stands for 100 ms, a starts word or an exception word
  other than at the handshake: one error line with status, starts,
  exception, step and error bits, and ->running false - the HDMI calls
  answer -ENODEV at once, standby is refused in prepare. A restart keeps
  magic, running bit and heartbeat; only the starts word shows it.
- new error bits (contract 5) and new error counts: a rate-limited
  warning naming the counter and its increase. The display MIPS's frame
  counts are normal traffic, not errors. What crust recorded before the
  handshake is reported once, at the first look.

Nothing is reloaded here; the work only reads SRAM, under the lock the
commands take, on the freezable workqueue so it stands still across a
standby. It is set up after the start of the firmware, so on removal devm
stops it before it undoes anything the start set up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
